{"id":"en-111","title":"OneLaser X Series Glossary | Machine Parts & Functions","family":"x-series","topic":"guides","read_minutes":1,"source_url":"https://wiki.1laser.com/en/x-series/glossary","source_updated_at":"2025-12-17T02:50:34.811Z","body_html":"<div><h2 id=\"x-series-glossary\"> X Series Glossary</h2>\n<p>The <strong>OneLaser X Series Glossary</strong> provides a clear explanation of the main components found on <a href=\"/#/article/en-21\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OneLaser X Series</a> laser engraving and cutting machines. This glossary helps users quickly understand the function of each part, supporting safe operation, troubleshooting, maintenance, and daily use.</p>\n<p>Whether you are a beginner or an experienced operator, this reference makes it easier to identify machine components and understand their roles during laser cutting and engraving workflows.</p>\n<h2 id=\"glossary-table\"> Glossary Table</h2>\n<figure><img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/x_series_glossary.jpg\" alt=\"OneLaser X Series Glossary\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\"></figure>\n<figure>\n  <table>\n    <thead>\n      <tr>\n        <th>No.</th>\n        <th>Component</th>\n        <th>Description</th>\n      </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr>\n        <td>1</td>\n        <td>Camera</td>\n        <td>Used to check the working status of the processing area.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>2</td>\n        <td>Laser Head</td>\n        <td>The component from which the laser beam is emitted.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>3</td>\n        <td>Touch Panel</td>\n        <td>Used to control the machine, including movement and running files.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>4</td>\n        <td>PM2.5 Detector</td>\n        <td>Detects temperature, humidity, and PM2.5 levels in the air.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>5</td>\n        <td>Function Panel</td>\n        <td>Used to connect external devices and the power cable.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>6</td>\n        <td>E-Stop (Emergency Stop)</td>\n        <td>Rapidly cuts off the power supply to the equipment in an emergency.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>7</td>\n        <td>Cooling Fan</td>\n        <td>Used to cool the rear cover of the machine.</td>\n      </tr>\n      <tr>\n        <td>8</td>\n        <td>Exhaust Vent</td>\n        <td>Used to connect the exhaust pipe.</td>\n      </tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</figure>\n</div>","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"x-series-glossary","text":"X Series Glossary"},{"level":2,"id":"glossary-table","text":"Glossary Table"}],"technical_version":"unknown"}